          "text": "the capacity we hold up front for a request \u2014 do we hand it back per request, or settle once the whole batch drains?"
         },
         {
          "author": "dario",
          "minute": "14:05",
          "text": "per request i think. sitting on it til the batch is done just starves everything at the tail"
         },
         {
          "author": "dermot",
          "minute": "14:07",
          "text": "mhm. and on a clean response we put the whole booking back?"
         },
         {
          "author": "dario",
          "minute": "14:09",
          "text": "no, only the gap honestly. what we booked for it vs what it actually spent, the difference is the part that goes back"
         },
         {
          "author": "emil",
          "minute": "14:11",
          "text": "so the booking was the ceiling and we're just returning what we over-reserved. sounds right"
         },
         {
          "author": "dario",
          "minute": "14:12",
          "text": "mhm, thats it"
         },
         {
          "author": "dermot",
          "minute": "14:14",
          "text": "then one that lands dead on its estimate returns nothing at all"
         },
         {
          "author": "dario",
          "minute": "14:16",
          "text": "right, nothing to give back there. best we can do until someone writes it"
