        "kind": "chat_thread",
        "participants": [
         "gideon",
         "dermot",
         "emil"
        ],
        "prompted_by": "A long online run the day before slowed to a crawl through the afternoon and came back to full speed only after a restart, so gideon starts digging into why effective concurrency decays over a run instead of holding steady.",
        "title": "throughput decaying over a long run, capacity never recovers without a restart",
        "messages": [
         {
          "author": "konrad",
          "minute": "14:12",
          "text": "viewer capacity has been sagging all week. by late afternoon its nowhere near where it starts"
         },
         {
          "author": "dermot",
          "minute": "14:18",
          "text": "mhm. i bounced it yesterday around 5 and it was back to full straight after"
         },
         {
          "author": "gideon",
          "minute": "14:23",
          "text": "so basically its the retries against that flaky endpoint. every cycle takes anohter reservation"
         },
         {
          "author": "konrad",
          "minute": "14:27",
          "text": "what happens to the one the failed attempt was already holding"
         },
         {
          "author": "gideon",
          "minute": "14:33",
          "text": "thats the thing, it never comes back. capacity just walks down all afternoon and stays down til we restart"
         },
         {
          "author": "dermot",
          "minute": "14:39",
          "text": "yeah ok. so the retry path is the one exit that doesnt let go of it"
         },
         {
          "author": "gideon",
          "minute": "14:45",
          "text": "ya. so it needs to hand it back there too, same as the other exits do. otherwise one endpoint flapping eats the whole day"
         }
        ],
        "pieces": [
         {
          "piece": "the problem is the retry cycles against that flaky endpoint",
          "carried_by": "gideon 14:23"
         },
         {
          "piece": "every retry cycle eats another reservation",
          "carried_by": "gideon 14:23"
         },
         {
          "piece": "the reservation the failed attempt held never comes back",
          "carried_by": "gideon 14:33"
         },
         {
          "piece": "capacity walks down all afternoon",
          "carried_by": "gideon 14:33"
         },
         {
          "piece": "it does not recover until a restart",
          "carried_by": "gideon 14:33"
         },
         {
          "piece": "corroboration that a restart restores it",
          "carried_by": "dermot 14:18"
         },
         {
          "piece": "observed symptom that raises the question: capacity far below its starting level by late afternoon",
          "carried_by": "konrad 14:12"
         },
         {
          "piece": "push on the unclear part - where the held reservation goes",
          "carried_by": "konrad 14:27"
         },
         {
          "piece": "the retry path is the exit that doesn't release it",
          "carried_by": "dermot 14:39"
         },
         {
          "piece": "settled: the retry path has to hand the reservation back like the other exits (not yet written)",
          "carried_by": "gideon 14:44"
         }
        ]
